course: dictionary
lesson: 3781
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Foot» is a good example. The words around it, the context, tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «Eagles are big birds of prey: hunters with hooked beaks, huge feet and amazing eyes.» Here feet are the body parts that birds stand and grip with. Ask: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «The shark was about 10 feet long.» Feet here is not about bodies at all. It is a unit of length, so 10 feet is about as long as three of your steps put together. «The lost puppy sat at the foot of the stairs» means the bottom of the stairs.
fact: A foot is a unit of length. There are 12 inches in a foot.
fact: A yard is 3 feet long, and feet is the plural of foot.
fact: «On foot» means walking, as in «We went to school on foot.»
fact: «Put your foot down» means be firm and not let something happen.
fact: «Foot the bill» is a verb phrase meaning to pay the bill.
exercise: «Butterflies taste with their feet.» What does feet mean in this sentence? | *Body parts they use to touch and taste things | Walking | The bottom of a hill | A unit of length, 12 inches
exercise: «The shark was about 10 feet long.» What does feet mean here? | *A unit of length, 12 inches | Walking | Parts of the body you stand on | The bottom of the sea
exercise: «The lost puppy sat at the foot of the stairs.» What does foot mean? | A part of your leg you stand on | 12 inches | The top | *The bottom
test: «We walked on foot to the shop.» What does on foot mean? | Riding in a car | Cycling fast | Swimming | *Walking
test: One foot is how many inches? | 10 | 24 | 16 | *12
exam: «Put your foot down, Mum said, and the children stopped arguing.» What does put your foot down mean? | *Be firm and not let something happen | Lift your foot up high | Run away from home | Stamp your foot hard on the floor
